{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2492 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "0f366dbe23cd6298d76c518d187d31187603f51cdf5c359028be5587b4edea54" :edb/db-before-t 2491 :edb/db-after-t 2492 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535804 50 #inst "2026-10-09T07:37:22.060Z" 13194139535804 true] [17592186166423 1100 "Find the maximum value of $Q(\\mathbf{x})=2x_1^2 - 5x_2^2 +3x_3^2$ given that $\\| \\mathbf{x} \\| =1$." 13194139535804 false] [17592186166423 1100 "Find the maximum value of $Q(\\mathbf{x})=2x_1^2 - 5x_2^2 +3x_3^2$ given that $\\| \\mathbf{x} \\| =1.$" 13194139535804 true] [17592186166423 1145 "First, notice that\n\n$$\nx_1^2 \\geq 0\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nx_2^2 \\geq 0\n$$\n\nSo, we have that\n\n$$\n2x_1^2 \\leq 3x_1^2, \\qquad -5x_2^2 \\leq 3x_2^2\n$$\n\nAs a result,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nQ(x) &= 2x_{1}^{2} - 5x_{2}^{2} + 3x_{3}^{2} \\\\\n&\\le 3x_{1}^{2} + 3x_{2}^{2} + 3x_{3}^{2} \\\\\n&= 3(x_{1}^{2} + x_{2}^{2} + x_{3}^{2})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that\n\n$$\n\\| \\mathbf{x} \\| = 1\n$$\n\nis equivalent to\n\n$$\nx_1^2 + x_2^2 + x_3^2 =1\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n3(x_{1}^{2} + x_{2}^{2} + x_{3}^{2}) = 3(1) = 3\n$$\n\nand, in turn,\n\n$$\nQ(\\mathbf{x}) \\leq 3\n$$\n\nSo, the value of $Q(\\mathbf{x})$ can be no greater than $3$. But before we conclude that $3$ is the maximum, we need to find a vector such that\n\n$$\nQ(\\mathbf{x}) = 3\n$$\n\nNotice that when $\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nQ(x) &= 2x_{1}^{2} - 5x_{2}^{2} + 3x_{3}^{2} \\\\\n&= 2(0)^{2} - 5(0)^{2} + 3(1)^{2} \\\\\n&= 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that\n\n$$\n\\| \\mathbf{x} \\| =1\n$$\n\nthe maximum value of $Q(\\mathbf{x})$ is equal to $3$." 13194139535804 false] [17592186166423 1145 "First, notice that $x_1^2 \\geq 0$ and $x_2^2 \\geq 0.$ So, we have that \n\n$$\n2x_1^2 \\leq 3x_1^2, \\qquad -5x_2^2 \\leq 3x_2^2.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-5{x}_{2}^{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & \\le 3{x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =3({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $\\| \\mathbf{x} \\| = 1$ is equivalent to $x_1^2 + x_2^2 + x_3^2 =1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2})=3(1)=3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(\\mathbf{x}) \\leq 3.$\n\nSo, the value of $Q(\\mathbf{x})$ can be no greater than $3.$ But before we conclude that $3$ is the maximum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(\\mathbf{x}) = 3.$\n\nNotice that when ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070559/assets/1986d7b40e318db91ac16ba9540ec704fd6221ac295dec66540c190a090a1463.png) we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-5{x}_{2}^{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =2(0)^{2}-5(0)^{2}+3(1)^{2} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that $\\| \\mathbf{x} \\| =1,$ the maximum value of $Q(\\mathbf{x})$ is equal to $3.$" 13194139535804 true] [17592186166424 1100 "Find the minimum value of $Q(\\mathbf{x})=5x_1^2 - 4x_2^2 - 6x_3^2$ given that $\\| \\mathbf{x} \\| =1$." 13194139535804 false] [17592186166424 1100 "Find the minimum value of $Q(\\mathbf{x})=5x_1^2 - 4x_2^2 - 6x_3^2$ given that $\\| \\mathbf{x} \\| =1.$" 13194139535804 true] [17592186166424 1145 "First, notice that\n\n$$\nx_1^2 \\geq 0\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nx_2^2 \\geq 0\n$$\n\nSo, we have that\n\n$$\n5x_1^2 \\geq -6x_1^2, \\qquad -4x_2^2 \\geq -6x_2^2\n$$\n\nAs a result,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nQ(x) &= 5x_{1}^{2} - 4x_{2}^{2} - 6x_{3}^{2} \\\\\n&\\ge - 6x_{1}^{2} - 6x_{2}^{2} - 6x_{3}^{2} \\\\\n&=-6(x_{1}^{2} + x_{2}^{2} + x_{3}^{2})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that\n\n$$\n\\| \\mathbf{x} \\| = 1\n$$\n\nis equivalent to\n\n$$\nx_1^2 + x_2^2 + x_3^2 =1\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n-6(x_{1}^{2} + x_{2}^{2} + x_{3}^{2}) =-6(1) =-6\n$$\n\nand, in turn,\n\n$$\nQ(\\mathbf{x}) \\geq -6\n$$\n\nSo, the value of $Q(\\mathbf{x})$ can be no smaller than $-6$. But before we conclude that $-6$ is the minimum, we need to find a vector such that\n\n$$\nQ(\\mathbf{x}) = -6\n$$\n\nNotice that when $\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nQ(x) &= 5x_{1}^{2} - 4x_{2}^{2} - 6x_{3}^{2} \\\\\n&= 5(0)^{2} - 4(0)^{2} - 6(1)^{2} \\\\\n&=-6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that\n\n$$\n\\| \\mathbf{x} \\| =1\n$$\n\nthe minimum value of $Q(\\mathbf{x})$ is equal to $-6$." 13194139535804 false] [17592186166424 1145 "First, notice that $x_1^2 \\geq 0$ and $x_2^2 \\geq 0.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n5x_1^2 \\geq -6x_1^2, \\qquad -4x_2^2 \\geq -6x_2^2.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =5{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{2}^{2}-6{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & \\ge -6{x}_{1}^{2}-6{x}_{2}^{2}-6{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =-6({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $\\| \\mathbf{x} \\| = 1$ is equivalent to $x_1^2 + x_2^2 + x_3^2 =1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2})=-6(1)=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(\\mathbf{x}) \\geq -6.$\n\nSo, the value of $Q(\\mathbf{x})$ can be no smaller than $-6.$ But before we conclude that $-6$ is the minimum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(\\mathbf{x}) = -6.$\n\nNotice that when ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070559/assets/d509eb79bc8d9a96b60922166e49d0225eac7a99d2614859c31af15199d4d47c.png) we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =5{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{2}^{2}-6{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =5(0)^{2}-4(0)^{2}-6(1)^{2} \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that $\\| \\mathbf{x} \\| =1,$ the minimum value of $Q(\\mathbf{x})$ is equal to $-6.$" 13194139535804 true] [17592186166425 1100 "Find the minimum value of $Q(\\mathbf{x})=x_1^2-2x_2^2-2x_3^2+2x_2x_3$  given that $\\| \\mathbf{x} \\| = 1.$" 13194139535804 true] [17592186166425 1100 "Find the minimum value of $Q(\\mathbf{x})=x_1^2-2x_2^2-2x_3^2+2x_2x_3$ given that $\\| \\mathbf{x} \\| = 1$." 13194139535804 false] [17592186166425 1145 "Let $A$ be the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form. Recall that:\n\n- The maximum value of $Q(\\mathbf{x})$, when $\\| \\mathbf{x} \\|=1$, is equal to the largest eigenvalue of $A{:}$\n$\\max \\{Q(\\mathbf{x}) \\: \\mid \\: \\| \\mathbf{x} \\| = 1 \\} = \\lambda_{\\textrm{max}}$\n- The minimum value of $Q(\\mathbf{x})$, when $\\| \\mathbf{x} \\|=1$, is equal to the smallest eigenvalue of $A{:}$\n$\\min \\{Q(\\mathbf{x}) \\: \\mid \\: \\| \\mathbf{x} \\| = 1 \\} = \\lambda_{\\textrm{min}}$\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix of our quadratic form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to calculate the eigenvalues of the matrix $A$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid A - λI \\mid &= 0 \\\\\n\\begin{vmatrix}1 - λ & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 - λ & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 - λ\\end{vmatrix} &= 0 \\\\\n(1 - λ)\\begin{vmatrix}-2 - λ & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2 - λ\\end{vmatrix} &= 0 \\\\\n(1 - λ)((-2 - λ)(-2 - λ) - 1) &= 0 \\\\\n(1 - λ)(λ^{2} + 4λ + 3) &= 0 \\\\\n(1 - λ)(λ + 3)(λ + 1) &= 0 \\\\\nλ &= 1,-1,-3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\min \\{Q(\\mathbf{x}) \\: \\mid \\: \\| \\mathbf{x} \\| = 1 \\} = -3\n$$" 13194139535804 false] [17592186166425 1145 "Let $A$ be the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form. Recall that: \n\n- The maximum value of $Q(\\mathbf{x}),$ when $\\| \\mathbf{x} \\|=1,$ is equal to the largest eigenvalue of $A{:}$\n\n$$\n\\max \\{ Q(\\mathbf{x}) \\: | \\:  \\| \\mathbf{x} \\| = 1 \\} = \\lambda_{\\textrm{max}}\n$$\n\n- The minimum value of $Q(\\mathbf{x}),$ when $\\| \\mathbf{x} \\|=1,$ is equal to the smallest eigenvalue of $A{:}$\n\n$$\n\\min \\{ Q(\\mathbf{x}) \\: | \\:  \\| \\mathbf{x} \\| = 1 \\} = \\lambda_{\\textrm{min}}\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix of our quadratic form:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070559/assets/d7716e2c2924212e880275dd674d4a951daf66ac41e5a888a57acb6be686118f.png)\n\nNow, we need to calculate the eigenvalues of the matrix $A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-2-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )((-2-\\lambda )(-2-\\lambda )-1) & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +3) & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )(\\lambda +3)(\\lambda +1) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =1,\\,-1,\\,-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\min \\{ Q(\\mathbf{x}) \\: | \\:  \\| \\mathbf{x} \\| = 1 \\} = -3.\n$$" 13194139535804 true] [17592186166822 1020 #edb/ref 17592186367078 13194139535804 true] [17592186166822 1020 #edb/ref 17592186367085 13194139535804 true] [17592186166822 1020 #edb/ref 17592186367148 13194139535804 true] [17592186166822 1020 #edb/ref 17592186367155 13194139535804 true] [17592186166822 1020 #edb/ref 17592186367162 13194139535804 true] [17592186166823 1020 #edb/ref 17592186367092 13194139535804 true] [17592186166823 1020 #edb/ref 17592186367099 13194139535804 true] [17592186166823 1020 #edb/ref 17592186367106 13194139535804 true] [17592186166823 1020 #edb/ref 17592186367169 13194139535804 true] [17592186166824 1020 #edb/ref 17592186367113 13194139535804 true] [17592186166824 1020 #edb/ref 17592186367120 13194139535804 true] [17592186166824 1020 #edb/ref 17592186367127 13194139535804 true] [17592186166824 1020 #edb/ref 17592186367134 13194139535804 true] [17592186166824 1020 #edb/ref 17592186367141 13194139535804 true] [17592186167039 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535804 true] [17592186167039 1100 "Find the minimum value of $Q(x) = 5x_{1}^{2} + 3x_{2}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖ = 1$." 13194139535804 false] [17592186167039 1100 "Find the minimum value of $Q(x)=5{x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" 13194139535804 true] [17592186167039 1145 "First, notice that ${x}_{1}^{2}\\ge 0.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n5{x}_{1}^{2}\\ge 3{x}_{1}^{2}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =5{x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & \\ge 3{x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =3({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $‖x‖=1$ is equivalent to ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}=1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2})=3(1)=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(x)\\ge 3.$ \n\nSo, the value of $Q(x)$ can be no smaller than $3.$ But before we conclude that $3$ is the minimum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(x)=3.$\n\nNotice that when  $x={[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{T},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =5{x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =5(0)+3(1)^{2} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that $‖x‖=1,$ the minimum value of $Q(x)$ is equal to $3.$" 13194139535804 true] [17592186367078 1017 #edb/ref 17592186367079 13194139535804 true] [17592186367078 1089 "q-138018" 13194139535804 true] [17592186367078 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535804 true] [17592186367078 1100 "Find the maximum value of $Q(x)=4{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" 13194139535804 true] [17592186367078 1113 #uuid "d163581a-379b-56c8-98a1-48aed6d35231" 13194139535804 true] [17592186367078 1145 "First, notice that ${x}_{2}^{2}\\ge 0.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n2{x}_{2}^{2}\\le 4{x}_{2}^{2}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =4{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & \\le 4{x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =4({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $‖x‖=1$ is equivalent to ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}=1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2})=4(1)=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(x)\\le 4.$\n\nSo, the value of $Q(x)$ can be no greater than $4.$ But before we conclude that $4$ is the maximum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(x)=4.$\n\nNotice that when  $x={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =4{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =4(1)^{2}+2(0)^{2} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that $‖x‖=1,$ the maximum value of $Q(x)$ is equal to $4.$" 13194139535804 true] [17592186367079 1000 #edb/ref 17592186367080 13194139535804 true] [17592186367079 1000 #edb/ref 17592186367081 13194139535804 true] [17592186367079 1000 #edb/ref 17592186367082 13194139535804 true] [17592186367079 1000 #edb/ref 17592186367083 13194139535804 true] [17592186367079 1000 #edb/ref 17592186367084 13194139535804 true] [17592186367079 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535804 true] [17592186367079 1041 "selection" 13194139535804 true] [17592186367079 1104 #edb/ref 17592186367083 13194139535804 true] [17592186367079 1110 #uuid "810d4f20-4fff-54ff-a388-dc08b8219321" 13194139535804 true] [17592186367080 1034 "3" 13194139535804 true] [17592186367080 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535804 true] [17592186367080 1111 #uuid "83813b32-f311-5992-b44c-076128c2c81d" 13194139535804 true] [17592186367081 1034 "8" 13194139535804 true] [17592186367081 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535804 true] [17592186367081 1111 #uuid "8441445f-64c5-5f3b-aac5-f12f05b4e46f" 13194139535804 true] [17592186367082 1034 "6" 13194139535804 true] [17592186367082 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535804 true] [17592186367082 1111 #uuid "11ea8215-c2b6-5b52-b3ef-7501347dd312" 13194139535804 true] [17592186367083 1034 "4" 13194139535804 true] [17592186367083 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535804 true] [17592186367083 1111 #uuid "eb5545d9-f3a7-52ee-aaa7-82fce7932a12" 13194139535804 true] [17592186367084 1034 "5" 13194139535804 true] [17592186367084 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535804 true] [17592186367084 1111 #uuid "50307521-32b9-5e89-ab20-d9b7f80322e3" 13194139535804 true] [17592186367085 1017 #edb/ref 17592186367086 13194139535804 true] [17592186367085 1089 "q-138023" 13194139535804 true] [17592186367085 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535804 true] [17592186367085 1100 "Find the maximum value of $Q(x)=2{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}-3{x}_{3}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" 13194139535804 true] [17592186367085 1113 #uuid 